<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name><![CDATA[Trans Canada Bike Route /Route Cyclable Transcanadienne - Map 1of4 - 2024 Proposed National Cycling Route Network for Canada & Accommodations POIs]]></name>
    <description><![CDATA[Website https://bikeacrosscanada.github.io/<br><br>Android App 'Trans Canada Bike Route App' <br>https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.wBikeAcrossCanadaRouteNetworkappv12_16984567<br><br>Trans Canada Bike Route.gpx  https://archive.org/download/BikeAcrossCanadaRouteNetworkGPSTracksPOIs/Trans%20Canada%20Bike%20Route.gpx<br>Trans Canada Bike Route.kmz  https://archive.org/download/BikeAcrossCanadaRouteNetworkGPSTracksPOIs/Trans%20Canada%20Bike%20Route.kmz<br><br>C1.gpx   https://archive.org/download/BikeAcrossCanadaRouteNetworkGPSTracksPOIs/C1.gpx <br>C1.kmz   https://archive.org/download/BikeAcrossCanadaRouteNetworkGPSTracksPOIs/C1.kmz<br><br>C2.gpx   https://archive.org/download/BikeAcrossCanadaRouteNetworkGPSTracksPOIs/C2.gpx<br>C2.kmz   https://archive.org/download/BikeAcrossCanadaRouteNetworkGPSTracksPOIs/C2.kmz<br><br>C3.gpx   https://archive.org/download/BikeAcrossCanadaRouteNetworkGPSTracksPOIs/C3.gpx<br>C3.kmz   https://archive.org/download/BikeAcrossCanadaRouteNetworkGPSTracksPOIs/C3.kmz<br><br>CN.gpx   https://archive.org/download/BikeAcrossCanadaRouteNetworkGPSTracksPOIs/CN.gpx<br>CN.kmz   https://archive.org/download/BikeAcrossCanadaRouteNetworkGPSTracksPOIs/CN.kmz<br><br>CA.gpx   https://archive.org/download/BikeAcrossCanadaRouteNetworkGPSTracksPOIs/CA.gpx<br>CA.kmz   https://archive.org/download/BikeAcrossCanadaRouteNetworkGPSTracksPOIs/CA.kmz<br><br>CW.gpx   https://archive.org/download/BikeAcrossCanadaRouteNetworkGPSTracksPOIs/CW.gpx<br>CW.kmz   https://archive.org/download/BikeAcrossCanadaRouteNetworkGPSTracksPOIs/CW.kmz<br><br>(currently viewing map) Part 1of4 (Containing the Route Network and Accommodations)<br> https://www.google.com/maps/d/viewer?mid=1NEEQLv7IXuf_KMahsVfYfvCD1WBA2F5K&vomp=1&cid=mp&cv=hsQgCD1sqp8.en.<br><br>Part 2of4  (containing various POIs (Points of Interest) from Airports to 'Warning Caution Notes')<br>https://www.google.com/maps/d/u/0/viewer?mid=1KcvDK_R8L5Akvhe1XgaQNGcgfPM5i8pi&ll=49.23214007847358%2C-91.52474924999999&z=3<br><br>Part 3of4 (containing more various POIs from 'Rest Areas' to 'Camera stop')<br>https://www.google.com/maps/d/viewer?mid=1BtLkN3ObsQmRsjqPcSOB1NqAbIL_Ajrp&ll=49.49730748105603%2C-91.4765404&z=3<br><br>Part 4of4 (extras -  incl. Campgrounds)<br>https://www.google.com/maps/d/viewer?mid=1EntCltrZkPPJ96A1apcLYSnJC31As5w&vomp=1&cid=mp&cv=HCuRaFymHmk.en.<br><br>2024 Trans Canada Bike Route (powered by the Bike Across Canada Route Network) is the Proposed National Cycling Route Network for Canada.  Data created from OpenStreetMap.<br><br>You can download the free Android App 'Trans Canada Bike Route App' which contains a zip with the the KMZ files and GPX files for viewing with the free  Android App 'Organic Maps offline Map' <br>https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.wBikeAcrossCanadaRouteNetworkappv12_16984567<br><br>The complete ZIP file for Viewing this mapset using the free 'Organic Maps offline map' smartphone App can be downloaded here<br>https://archive.org/download/BikeAcrossCanadaRouteNetworkGPSTracksPOIs/Bike%20Across%20Canada%20Route%20Network%20KMZ%20-%20extracts%20from%20GPX%20file%20ZIP%20file.zip<br><br>The latest version of the GPX file can be viewed here (best viewed with the free Garmin Basecamp desktop software, to see all the layers and copy what you want for trip planning)<br>https://archive.org/download/BikeAcrossCanadaRouteNetworkGPSTracksPOIs/Bike%20Across%20Canada%20Route%20Network%20W-E%20%28proposed%29%20Connected%20daily%20OSM%20data%20segments.gpx<br><br>Join the conversation on Facebook www.facebook.com/bikeacrosscanada <br><br>(Also, the 'Trans Canada Bike Route Approved Mapbook' Google Presentation can be viewed here)<br>https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1g9avuYgJtpFtvTe7v9kItrWzrNGR9z0VRjifzCN6ZOw/edit?usp=sharing <br><br>The source of the network came from overlapping the GPS tracks from those who have done the trip, and connecting the end of day locations of trips (without GPS tracks), organized into 14 regional maps, with the Great Big List map as an overview map.  <br>https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=1g2y8npEN_VVyzMK4G0FWjEk8WSU&ll=55.696107950999306%2C-127.6562573154327&z=5]]></description>
