      <Placemark>
        <name>Columbia Icefield Campground</name>
        <description><![CDATA[description: Open: June 12 to October 14, 2024<br><br>"Icefield Tent<br><br>Down the road from the world-renowned Columbia Icefield, this campground puts you on the doorstep of some of the most spectacular scenery on the planet. Glacier views are had from most campsites and from the windows of the cozy log cookhouses.<br><br>Tenting only."<br>https://parks.canada.ca/pn-np/ab/jasper/activ/passez-stay/camping?utm_source=gmb&utm_medium=columbia_campground<br><br>Type: National Park Campground<br>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1765-817717</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="description">
            <value><![CDATA[Open: June 12 to October 14, 2024

"Icefield Tent

Down the road from the world-renowned Columbia Icefield, this campground puts you on the doorstep of some of the most spectacular scenery on the planet. Glacier views are had from most campsites and from the windows of the cozy log cookhouses.

Tenting only."
https://parks.canada.ca/pn-np/ab/jasper/activ/passez-stay/camping?utm_source=gmb&utm_medium=columbia_campground
]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Type">
            <value>National Park Campground
</value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            -117.2045656,52.2200725,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>*Jonas Creek Campground</name>
        <description><![CDATA[description: Open: June 5 to September 9, 2024<br>"Campsite #14 is designated for bike camping only."<br>https://parks.canada.ca/pn-np/ab/jasper/activ/passez-stay/camping#jonas<br>National Park Campground<br>"Reservable: All sites available on a First Come, First Served basis. No reservations possible."<br>"cooking shelter"<br>"A night at Jonas can be spent camping within earshot of the babbling creek. Hardy campers looking to get away from it all can also walk into hillside sites secluded in the forest. In addition, a bike camping area can be found near the cooking shelter, offering a great stop-over option for cyclists tackling the length of the Icefields Parkway.<br><br>Campsite #14 is designated for bike camping only. This is a shared site for unsupported bike touring and can accommodate 10 tents.<br><br>Best suited for tents as well as motorhomes and trailers under 25 feet"<br><br>Type: Approved Accommodation (campground)]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1502-FFEA00</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="description">
            <value><![CDATA[Open: June 5 to September 9, 2024
"Campsite #14 is designated for bike camping only."
https://parks.canada.ca/pn-np/ab/jasper/activ/passez-stay/camping#jonas
National Park Campground
"Reservable: All sites available on a First Come, First Served basis. No reservations possible."
"cooking shelter"
"A night at Jonas can be spent camping within earshot of the babbling creek. Hardy campers looking to get away from it all can also walk into hillside sites secluded in the forest. In addition, a bike camping area can be found near the cooking shelter, offering a great stop-over option for cyclists tackling the length of the Icefields Parkway.

Campsite #14 is designated for bike camping only. This is a shared site for unsupported bike touring and can accommodate 10 tents.

Best suited for tents as well as motorhomes and trailers under 25 feet"
]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Type">
            <value>Approved Accommodation (campground)</value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            -117.3964765,52.4173904,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Honeymoon Lake Campground (Jasper National Park)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[description: "<br>Honeymoon Lake<br><br> Open: May 15 to September 9, 2024<br> Reservable: All sites available on a First Come, First Served basis. No reservations possible.<br> Sites: 34<br><br> Fees: See full list of camping fees here<br> Site type:<br> Unserviced, with fire pit<br> Bike camping (campsite #24 only)<br><br>Being able to replace ringing phones, noisy traffic and city smog with quiet lakeside strolls and the smell of breakfast cooking over a campfire gives you a sense of how Honeymoon Lake Campground got its name.<br><br>Campsite #24 is designated for bike camping only. This is a shared site for unsupported bike touring and can accommodate 6 tents.<br><br>Best suited for tents as well as motorhomes and trailers under 27 feet"<br>https://parks.canada.ca/pn-np/ab/jasper/activ/passez-stay/camping#honeymoon<br>National Park Campground<br><br>Type: Approved Accommodation (campground)]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1502-FFEA00</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="description">
            <value><![CDATA["
Honeymoon Lake

 Open: May 15 to September 9, 2024
 Reservable: All sites available on a First Come, First Served basis. No reservations possible.
 Sites: 34

 Fees: See full list of camping fees here
 Site type:
 Unserviced, with fire pit
 Bike camping (campsite #24 only)

Being able to replace ringing phones, noisy traffic and city smog with quiet lakeside strolls and the smell of breakfast cooking over a campfire gives you a sense of how Honeymoon Lake Campground got its name.

Campsite #24 is designated for bike camping only. This is a shared site for unsupported bike touring and can accommodate 6 tents.

Best suited for tents as well as motorhomes and trailers under 27 feet"
https://parks.canada.ca/pn-np/ab/jasper/activ/passez-stay/camping#honeymoon
National Park Campground
]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Type">
            <value>Approved Accommodation (campground)</value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            -117.6813985,52.5558106,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
