      <Placemark>
        <name>Mount Kerkeslin Campground</name>
        <description><![CDATA[description: Open: May 29 to September 2, 2024<br> Reservable: All sites available on a First Come, First Served basis. No reservations possible.<br> Sites: 42<br><br> Fees: See full list of camping fees here<br> Site type:<br> Unserviced, with fire pit<br><br>This shaded campground is an excellent stop-over for tenters and RVers looking for peace and quiet along the Icefields Parkway. Located along the Athabasca River, it is just a short drive from the iconic Athabasca Falls and only 34 km from the town of Jasper.<br><br>Best suited for tents as well asmotorhomes and trailers under 27 feet.<br>"<br>https://parks.canada.ca/pn-np/ab/jasper/activ/passez-stay/camping#kerkeslin<br>Type: National Park Campground<br>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1765-817717</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="description">
            <value><![CDATA[Open: May 29 to September 2, 2024
 Reservable: All sites available on a First Come, First Served basis. No reservations possible.
 Sites: 42

 Fees: See full list of camping fees here
 Site type:
 Unserviced, with fire pit

This shaded campground is an excellent stop-over for tenters and RVers looking for peace and quiet along the Icefields Parkway. Located along the Athabasca River, it is just a short drive from the iconic Athabasca Falls and only 34 km from the town of Jasper.

Best suited for tents as well asmotorhomes and trailers under 27 feet.
"
https://parks.canada.ca/pn-np/ab/jasper/activ/passez-stay/camping#kerkeslin]]></value>
          </Data>
